WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.575
Diabetic retinopathy screening in primary care.

2
00:00:04.025 --> 00:00:09.365
Setting up retinal screening, grading results and agreeing referral thresholds with eye services.

3
00:00:09.815 --> 00:00:14.436
Regular retinal photography detects sight-threatening disease before symptoms appear.

4
00:00:14.886 --> 00:00:18.694
Screening intervals depend on previous results and glycaemic control.

5
00:00:19.144 --> 00:00:23.951
Better control of glucose, blood pressure and lipids reduces the risk of progression.

6
00:00:24.401 --> 00:00:29.857
Rapid falls in HbA1c can transiently worsen retinopathy and need closer review.

7
00:00:30.307 --> 00:00:35.625
Central-involving oedema with reduced vision is usually treated with intravitreal therapy.

8
00:00:36.075 --> 00:00:39.523
Laser and steroids remain options in selected patients.
